1. DEFINITIONS

   1.1 "Software" means the Lutier synthesizer engine, its source code,
       compiled binaries, the .synth and .score domain-specific languages,
       the parser, the audio engine, presets, example files, documentation,
       and any other file distributed in this repository, in whole or in
       part, in original or modified form.

   1.2 "System" means the Software together with any derivative work,
       fork, port, rewrite, wrapper, plugin, library binding, hosted
       service, API, application, or other mechanism that incorporates,
       embeds, calls, or is substantially based on the Software or on its
       languages, algorithms, or design.

   1.3 "Output" means any audio content (including but not limited to WAV,
       MP3, or any other rendered audio), music, sound effect, or
       composition generated by the Software, as well as .synth and
       .score files, regardless of who or what authored them.

   1.4 "Larger Work" means a work whose primary offering to its audience
       is NOT the audio itself: for example a game, film, video,
       animation, podcast, advertisement, software application, live
       performance, or theater piece, in which Outputs appear as
       soundtrack, sound effects, or accompaniment.

   1.5 "Substantial Human Transformation" means creative reworking of an
       Output performed by a human, in which the human contribution is
       significant enough that the resulting work is a new musical work
       and not a repackaging of the Output. Section 5.4 defines what does
       and does not qualify.

   1.6 "Licensor" means the copyright holder identified above.

   1.7 "You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights under
       this License.

   1.8 "Commercial Use" means any use primarily intended for or directed
       toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including but
       not limited to: selling, licensing for a fee, renting, charging for
       access, running paid services, monetizing via advertising,
       subscriptions, credits, donations tied to access, streaming
       royalties, or using the Software, System, or Outputs as part of a
       product or service that generates revenue.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS (SOFTWARE)

   Subject to the terms of this License, the Licensor grants You a
   worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to:

   a) use, run, copy, and study the Software for personal, educational,
      research, and other NON-commercial purposes;
   b) modify the Software and create derivative works, for NON-commercial
      purposes only;
   c) redistribute the Software or derivative works, free of charge only,
      provided that this License and the attribution required in Section 4
      accompany every copy.

3. PROHIBITED USES (SOFTWARE AND SYSTEM)

   You may NOT, under any circumstances, without prior written permission
   from the Licensor:

   a) sell, resell, license for a fee, rent, lease, or otherwise
      commercialize the Software or the System, in whole or in part;
   b) offer the Software or System as a paid product or paid service of
      any kind, including but not limited to: SaaS, web service, API,
      plugin, mobile or desktop application, marketplace item, or
      "music generation" service, whether paid directly, by subscription,
      by credits, by advertising, by donations tied to access, or by any
      other monetization model;
   c) operate any product, service, store, catalog, library, channel, or
      pipeline — manual or automated — whose offering to third parties
      is, in substance, audio produced by the Software or System,
      whether sold, licensed, streamed for revenue, or otherwise
      monetized;
   d) use the Software or System internally within a for-profit product
      pipeline whose offering to customers is, in substance, the
      generation or provision of audio produced by the Software;
   e) remove, hide, or alter copyright notices, this License, or the
      attribution required in Section 4;
   f) sublicense the Software or System under different terms, including
      relicensing derivative works under permissive or commercial
      licenses;
   g) circumvent or attempt to circumvent any restriction of this License
      by technical, formal, or contractual means, including interposing
      third parties, shell entities, chained licenses, or cosmetic
      alterations to Outputs (see Section 5.4).

4. ATTRIBUTION (MANDATORY — SOFTWARE, SYSTEM, AND OUTPUTS)

   4.1 Software and System. Any use, copy, modification, or
       redistribution of the Software or System MUST:
       a) keep the notice "Copyright (c) 2026 C3B" and a copy of this
          License in all copies of the source code;
       b) in any public project, application, video, article, or material
          that uses or is based on the Software, include visible credit
          in the form given in Section 4.3, with a link to
          https://github.com/ctresb when the medium allows;
       c) not suggest that the Licensor endorses You or Your use.

   4.2 Outputs. Any public use of Outputs — commercial or not, inside a
       Larger Work or not — MUST credit the Software. The credit must
       appear where credits are customarily given for that medium (game
       credits screen, film/video credits, video description, album
       liner notes / track description, podcast notes, etc.).

   4.3 Credit template. Use one of the following (or an equivalent
       translation), verbatim or adapted to the medium:

       English:
         "Music made with Lutier, by C3B — github.com/ctresb"
       Short form (space-constrained media):
         "Music: Lutier (github.com/ctresb)"
       Portuguese:
         "Músicas feitas com o Lutier, de C3B — github.com/ctresb"
       Short form:
         "Músicas: Lutier (github.com/ctresb)"

       When only sound effects are used, "Music" may read "Audio" /
       "Áudio". The link may be omitted only where the medium cannot
       carry links or URLs at all (e.g., radio); the names "Lutier" and
       "C3B" may never be omitted.

5. OUTPUTS — WHAT YOU MAY AND MAY NOT DO

   5.1 Ownership. The Licensor claims no copyright over the creative
       choices You make in Your .synth/.score compositions. However, Your
       rights to USE Outputs are governed by this Section, and any use of
       Outputs outside these permissions is a breach of this License.

   5.2 PERMITTED — non-commercial use. You may use, share, and publish
       Outputs freely for non-commercial purposes, with the attribution
       of Section 4.2.

   5.3 PERMITTED — Outputs inside a Larger Work (commercial). You may
       commercialize a Larger Work that CONTAINS Outputs — e.g., sell a
       game, film, or app whose soundtrack was made with the Software —
       with no royalties owed, provided:
       a) the attribution of Section 4.2 is present; and
       b) the audio is an integrated component of the Larger Work, not
          its primary offering. Selling or separately monetizing the
          soundtrack detached from the Larger Work (e.g., a standalone
          OST album) falls under Section 5.4, not this Section.

   5.4 PERMITTED — standalone music, ONLY with Substantial Human
       Transformation. You may sell or monetize standalone music (tracks,
       beats, albums, stock/library music, streaming releases) that
       INCORPORATES Outputs only if the final work results from
       Substantial Human Transformation, cumulatively:
       a) a human personally performed the reworking, exercising real
          creative judgment (composition, arrangement, performance,
          layering with material of the human's own authorship);
       b) the Output is a component of the new work, not its substance —
          a listener comparing the two would recognize a materially new
          musical work, not the Output with cosmetic changes; and
       c) the transformation was done individually per work, not by any
          automated, scripted, batch, or mass process.

       The following are, without limitation, NOT Substantial Human
       Transformation, alone or combined:
         - changing parameters, presets, seed, tempo, pitch, key, or
           mix settings and re-rendering;
         - trimming, looping, slicing, rearranging, or crossfading
           segments of Outputs;
         - applying effects, mastering, EQ, compression, reverb, or
           format conversion;
         - overlaying minor elements (a sample, a vocal tag, a single
           extra layer) on an otherwise intact Output;
         - any edit performed by automated or AI-driven tooling in bulk;
         - any workflow whose purpose or effect is to produce sellable
           audio from the Software at scale.

       Burden of demonstration: in case of dispute, You must be able to
       show the human creative process (project files, stems, drafts)
       that produced the transformation.

   5.5 FORBIDDEN — everything else. In particular You may NOT:
       a) sell, license, or monetize Outputs as-is or with changes below
          the threshold of Section 5.4 — including selling beats, stock
          music, NFTs, sample packs, or streaming releases of raw or
          cosmetically altered Outputs;
       b) monetize Outputs through intermediaries or automation to
          simulate compliance (e.g., auto-slicing Outputs into "samples",
          bulk-uploading variations to streaming platforms, laundering
          Outputs through third parties or successive licenses);
       c) claim that Outputs are free of this License or relicense them
          in a way that removes the conditions of Sections 4 and 5.

   5.6 Examples (illustrative, not limiting):
       - Developer composes soundtrack with Lutier, sells the game, puts
         the Section 4.3 credit in the credits screen — ALLOWED.
       - Producer takes a Lutier Output, adds original vocals, rewrites
         the arrangement, records live instruments over it, releases the
         song commercially with credit — ALLOWED under 5.4.
       - Person generates a track, changes two settings or trims the
         intro, and sells it as a beat — FORBIDDEN (5.4, cosmetic).
       - Person scripts Lutier to render 500 tracks, slices them into
         loops, and sells the pack claiming "editing" — FORBIDDEN
         (5.4(c), 5.5(b)).
       - Company runs a paid site that generates music with Lutier —
         FORBIDDEN (3(b)-(c)).
       - Selling the game's OST as a standalone album of raw Outputs —
         FORBIDDEN unless each track meets 5.4 or a separate license is
         obtained (Section 10).

6. CONTRIBUTIONS

   Unless You state otherwise in writing, any contribution intentionally
   submitted by You for inclusion in the Software is licensed to the
   Licensor under the terms of this License, and You grant the Licensor
   the right to use, modify, and distribute it as part of the Software.

7. TERMINATION

   Any breach of this License automatically terminates Your rights under
   it, including the permissions of Section 5 for Outputs already
   produced. Rights may be reinstated, at the Licensor's sole discretion,
   once the breach is cured. Sections 4, 5, 8, and 9 survive termination.

8. NO WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
   OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

9. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR
   OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE,
   ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR
   OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

10. COMMERCIAL LICENSING

   Uses forbidden by Sections 3 and 5 may be negotiated individually.
   Contact the Licensor (github.com/ctresb) for a separate commercial
   license.

11. INTERPRETATION

   Where this License is ambiguous, it shall be interpreted in the manner
   most restrictive to commercialization of the Software, System, and
   Outputs, consistent with the intent stated here: the only permitted
   monetization paths are Sections 5.3 (Outputs inside a Larger Work) and
   5.4 (Substantial Human Transformation), always with attribution.

